# Day 25/50 — Processes

Opening a browser, playing music or running a program — each of these can involve a process.

A **process** is a program in execution
It has its own state and resources, such as memory and system information.

A program is just a set of instructions stored somewhere. 
A process is what happens when those instructions actually start running.

And that difference is interesting.

Having a plan and putting it into action are two very different things.

An idea can exist for a long time without becoming anything real.

**Because a program becomes a process only when it starts doing something**
